On 11/21/12 18:41, Vasiliy Tolstov wrote:
> Another test has very bad results:
> initiator multipath -ll running than storage go to down never returns
> (deadlock), but other multipath -ll returns immediate with output (i'm
> reboot sas01)

It could be helpful to have a look at the call stacks generated by "echo 
w >/proc/sysrq-trigger". If this output reveals that device removal 
triggers hanging I/O then that might indicate that one or more SCSI 
device removal patches have not yet been backported to SLES 11 SP2. Have 
you already tried whether the same test succeeds with kernel 3.6.7 ? 
Several SCSI device removal fixes have been integrated in kernel 3.6.

Bart.

